This repository holds content under two licences.

1. The code (*.py): the MIT License, below.

2. Content from the logs of "Sparks of Weight-Space Programming: LLMs can natively read & write neural network
   weights" (Rikiya Takehi, Jayden Teoh, Alex Zhang and Omar Khattab; https://github.com/RikiyaT/lm_understand-logs),
   and the model outputs in runs/: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0),
   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode. This content is
   - specs/astra_breakout_strategy.txt: the paragraph that opens Astra's Breakout answer, unchanged;
   - specs/astra_breakout_wiring.txt: Astra's Breakout edits block, with every value replaced by a placeholder;
   - prompts/: the authors' Experiment 1 and 2 prompts, adapted to show footprint tables in place of the weights.
   The model outputs in runs/ are released under CC BY 4.0 as far as we hold any rights in them.

MinAtar's source code (GPL-3.0) is not included. The prompts that quote it are rebuilt at run time from
https://github.com/alan-turing-institute/weights_editing.

